A timer line that fires stays armed.
It would signal again on every later tick;
after a tick no Irq armed on a timer line is due.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -326,7 +326,7 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
             continue;
         }
         if (irq_due(irq, sched_ticks)) {
-            irq_signal(irq);
+            sched_signal(irq_notification(irq), irq->bits);
         } else if (tick_before(irq->deadline, nearest)) {
             nearest = irq->deadline;
         }
